  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Humanitarian Assistance in Food aid for IDPs in Mvolo and Mundri East County</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The aim of this project is to develop the capacity of Caritas Yei (the development wing of Catholic Diocese of Yei) to provide humanitarian food aid assistance to the displaced IDPs in Mvolo and Mundri East County Western Equatoria State South Sudan. The project will also revitalize Caritas Yei which has been redundant for the last two years enabling it to respond to the anticipated emergency situations in the country, including any scenarios that develop during the build up to the referendum and the aftermath of the Referenda and any other natural or man made disasters.  

The overall Objective is; To strengthen the capacity of caritas Yei in providing food relief assistance to the current displaced community in Mvolo and Mundri East and be able to respond to any other humanitarian crisis that might affect the diocese. This intervention will focus on provision of food aid assistance to the IDPs in Mvolo and Mundri East Counties under WFP support. 
The expected results are; Caritas Yei be able to recruit 2 storekeepers, 1 Administration and finance assistance and 1 field officer, Distribute a total of 143.52 metric tone of food in two months (November-December 2010) to a total of 4,227 beneficiaries in Mvolo and Mundri East.

The direct beneficiaries of the project will be the 4,227 IDPs beneficiaries verified and registered by WFP in Mvolo and Mundri (3,205 in Mvolo centre &amp; 1,022 beneficiaries in Witto Mundri East County. The 4 recruited and trained staff of Caritas Yei (2 storekeepers and 1 field officer based in Mundri-Mvolo and 1 Admin/Finance assistant based in Yei) well motivated and able to take the task of food aid distribution timely and effectively to the targeted beneficiaries in the two Counties of Mvolo and Mundri are expected to benefit. 

The contribution from CAFOD to the overall project will cover salaries for the 4 staff, support office, vehicle and general administration running cost, training and field operation support as detailed in the budget. WFP will provide in-kind food rations and a cash contribution at $51.51 per metrix tonne distributed.

CAFOD is already a twinning partner with the dioceses of Yei under EA12/2010 Appeal. This project support will therefore build on the existing programme and strengthen the current relationship and provide additional capacity to emergency appeal EA12/2010. EA12/2010 over all objective in preparing the diocese of Yei to be able to respond effectively and timely will be enhanced with the support of this project.</narrative>
  </description>
